`src/components/ErrorBoundary.tsx` — class component (required for `componentDidCatch`).

**Usage:**

```tsx
// Default fallback
<ErrorBoundary>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>

// Custom fallback
<ErrorBoundary fallback={(error, retry) => (
  <div>
    <p>{error.message}</p>
    <button onClick={retry}>Try again</button>
  </div>
)}>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>
```

Key details:
- `getDerivedStateFromError` captures the error and triggers the fallback render
- `componentDidCatch` logs `message`, `stack`, and React's `componentStack` to the console
- `retry` resets state to `null`, causing React to re-render children from scratch
- Accepts an optional `fallback` render prop for custom UI; defaults to a minimal built-in fallback
